# A Compile game, written down move by move.
#
# Lines that are not comments are commands, exactly as they are typed at the
# prompt. Undo and redo are moves like any other, so reading this file back
# retraces the game as it was really played - second thoughts and all - and
# arrives at the same position it was saved from.
#
# The deal line says how many were playing, what they were dealt from, and who
# was in each seat - 'you' for a person here, a skill for the program.
#
#   dotnet run -- compile replay <this file>

deal 2 639223718171400303 you you

#   1  turn 1, Player 1
draft love
#      Player 1 drafts Love.

#   2  turn 2, Player 2
draft metal
#      Player 2 drafts Metal.

#   3  turn 3, Player 2
draft life
#      Player 2 drafts Life.

#   4  turn 4, Player 1
draft death
#      Player 1 drafts Death.

#   5  turn 5, Player 1
draft fire
#      Player 1 drafts Fire.

#   6  turn 6, Player 2
draft water
#      Player 2 drafts Water.
#      The draft is over. Both players now set their 3 protocols against the 3 lines, face down.

#   7  turn 7, Player 1
arrange love death fire
#      Player 1 sets Love, Death, Fire against lines 1 to 3.

#   8  turn 8, Player 2
arrange metal life water
#      Player 2 sets Metal, Life, Water against lines 1 to 3.
#      Both are turned over at once - Player 1 has Love, Death, Fire; Player 2 has Metal, Life, Water.
#      Both decks are shuffled - 18 cards each - and 5 drawn.

#   9  turn 9, Player 1
choose fire-4
#      That is not what the game is asking for - cards are being played: say a card and a line, like 'fire-3 2'.

#  10  turn 9, Player 1
play fire-4 2
#      Fire-4 cannot go face up on line 2. Fire is on line 3 - or play it face down anywhere, for 2.

#  11  turn 9, Player 1
play fire-4 3
#      Player 1 plays Fire-4 to line 3.
#      Fire-4 asks Player 1 to choose.

#  12  turn 9, Player 1
choose love-1
#      Player 1 discards Love-1.

#  13  turn 9, Player 1
yes
#      Fire-4 asks Player 1 to choose.

#  14  turn 9, Player 1
choose death-2
#      Player 1 discards Death-2.

#  15  turn 9, Player 1
no
#      Player 1 says no, so nothing waiting on that happens.
#      Player 1 draws 3.

#  16  turn 10, Player 2
play life-2 2
#      Player 2 plays Life-2 to line 2.
#      Player 2 draws a card.
#      Life-2 finds nothing to do.

#  17  turn 11, Player 1
play love-6 1
#      Player 1 plays Love-6 to line 1.
#      Player 2 draws 2.

#  18  turn 12, Player 2
play life-3 2
#      Player 2 plays Life-3 to line 2.
#      Water-5 asks Player 2 to choose.

#  19  turn 12, Player 2
choose water-4
#      Player 2 discards Water-4.

#  20  turn 13, Player 1
resign
#      The game is over: Player 1 walked away.

